1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,300
My mum doesn't know CAD
or 3D printers.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,700
She just talks to Mıstık.

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:10,800
Mum: Mıstık, can you print me
a little gift box for flowers?

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,000
Mıstık: Mum, I found two.
1) Flower box, 2 h 16 min

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,400
2) Plant pot, 4 h 34 min.
Which one?

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,700
Mum: The first one, a white box.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Mum: Lovely, print it please!

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,200
[Blocked: owner approval needed]

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:27,600
Mıstık: Queued, and I told the owner.
The owner decides when it starts.

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,200
[Owner's chat: Mum asks to start #7]

11
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,300
Owner approves: Started #7.

12
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,100
The rules are in code.
Only the owner starts. Anyone can stop.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,200
A watcher checks the printer
every two minutes.

14
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,300
No model calls, no tokens.

15
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,900
It writes only when something happens.

16
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:48,100
At the end, the bed cools and
the printer pushes the part off.

17
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:52,700
Mıstık: Mum, the flower box is done.
It dropped off: take it from the box.

18
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,900
[To the owner: details and a photo]

19
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:58,400
We asked it to clear the plate
without a person.

20
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:01,700
It tried a push,
and the part got stuck at the front.

21
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,600
It found a tilted base
and printed its own upgrade.

22
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,800
The plugin makes this a rule:

23
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,600
when a human task repeats,
it proposes an upgrade.

24
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:15,000
No printer?
Try it with the simulator.

25
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:19,800
Install it with --enable,
then run: hermes home3d demo

26
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:25,000
Mıstık.
The home's 3D workshop.
